# MCSP Kernel Assembly ABI Reconciliation 0.59

Status: Constructive reconciliation
Qualification: Verified within bounded Linux x86-64 fixture
Parent: CONTROLLED-DEVICE-INTERACTION-0.58.mcsp

## Purpose

Remove the explicit 0.58 objtool/MITIGATION_RETHUNK residue without changing the
MCSP semantic obligation.

MCSP remains its own kernel:

    MCSP KERNEL = DETERMINATE CONDITION

Linux x86-64 kernel ABI/hardening conventions are realization constraints only.

## Reconciliation

Kernel-facing MCSP assembly functions use:
- ELF FUNC symbol with explicit size;
- __x86_return_thunk for the Linux x86-64 return projection;
- non-executable GNU stack note.

The 0.58 observation relation remains unchanged:

    (observed_value & 0xffff) == 0x00ed

No new STATE, TYPE, device operation, or semantic primitive is introduced.

## Qualification

0.59 requires:
1. warning-free Kbuild/objtool;
2. sized FUNC symbols for identity and observation predicates;
3. relocations to __x86_return_thunk;
4. unchanged isolated EDU read-only observation;
5. no host module insertion.

This reconciliation is bounded to the tested Linux x86-64 kernel configuration.
